<title>GERMANY: German cocoa grind 11.71 pct lower in Q1, 1997.</title>
<headline>German cocoa grind 11.71 pct lower in Q1, 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German cocoa grind dropped by 11.71 percent to 61,379.3 tonnes in the first quarter of 1997 from 69,520.3 tonnes in the same 1996 period, the German Confectionery Industry Association BDS said on Monday.</p>
<p>Analysts last week estimated the first quarter data to be down at perhaps 60,000 tonnes, citing extremely high year-ago figures.</p>
<p>The German grind in the fourth 1996 quarter was 56,254.7 tonnes, which was down 21.2 percent from the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
